cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the v3 result release.
  Protocol v1 is invalidated and its numbers may not be cited. Protocol v2 is
  superseded: two of its five headline claims reverse under budget-matched
  controls, and it carries an errata file — cite it only when discussing those
  errata. Once the master paper — "After 2022: Japan's Search for a Novel
  Foreign Policy", of which this repository is the Chapter-4 evidence — is
  published, please cite that instead and this repository in addition.
title: "Neural Architecture Search with Backprop: a reconstruction of Backprop-NEAT as a preregistered experiment"
abstract: >-
  A NumPy reconstruction of David Ha's Backprop-NEAT (2016), audited against
  hardmaru/backprop-neat-js and run as a sequence of frozen, preregistered
  protocols. Protocol v3 treats the implementation details as the experiment:
  1,920 runs over 30 paired replicates and five 2-D geometries, measuring the
  inner learner's stopping rule, forward-pass scheduling, the selection operator
  and weight inheritance, and reporting which of v2's headline claims survive
  which evaluator setting. Two of five reverse. Every published number
  regenerates byte-identically from committed raw records. Experiment 2 of three
  in a research line on evolutionary search for open-world decision problems.
